@Node Intro "--> Features <--"

 Some days ago other members meant that we should release something now, so
 I wrote the docs to this util now. I coded the util over a month ago but
 never released it coz I was to busy to write the docs. I invested all my
 time in learning C, so all my new doors/utils will be in C now.

 * enter users handle and the doors searches for his New User Answers
   and display them
 * displays TempAnswers on a node you want
 * running on all /X Systems I think
 * no backdoors
 * compiled AREXX (if you have no CoProz contact me and you get a running
   version for your system)


                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Install "--> Installation <--"

 Extract the whole User Answer Shower archive to your assigned doors dir.

 /X2.x: Append the following Line to your
        BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD File:
        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------
        answer        RM200DOORS:Answer/Answer.exe
        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------

 /X3.x: For installing on that systems make your own Icon and place it
        in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD drawer.

 Copy the rexxsupport.library to your Libs directory.

 Be sure, that you have the following files: (otherwise the door won`t work)

 * TempAns in the BBS:NodeX dirs
 * Answers in the BBS:NodeX dirs

                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@Node Instr "--> Instruction <--"

 When you started the door, you will be asked if you wanna see a Tempans
 file of a node or search for a User in the Answer files(s).
 If you choosed `t` for the TempAns file, the door will ask for the node.
 When you entered it it will display it.
 If you choosed `a` for, the door will ask for the users handle. When you
 entered it, it will ask from which node he should start to search. Enter
 the node and the door will search and display the answers if found.


                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}
@endnode

